{
  "id": 98287262,
  "iid": 2901,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "fix #17369 tshark json now handles mixed children",
  "description": "tshark's JSON export used to assume that all nodes from a certain parent\nhave the same 'shape' - they all have children, or none have children.\nThis does not necessarily hold when the --no-duplicate-keys option is\nactivated: in that case, nodes with the same field name will be merged,\nand we end up sometimes with fields containing arrays of mixed element\ntypes (some having children, some not). When that happened, the output\nused to be coerced to the element type of the first element of the list.\nNow we check the element type for each element of the list, ensuring a\nvalid output.\n\nIn the bug I considered rather modifying how the --no-duplicate-keys processes items, or maybe what kind of elements the http2 plugin generates. This patch goes with the approach of making the final JSON generation handle this specific case.\n\nBefore the change, for the example in #17369, we generate the following JSON:\n\n`\"http2\": [\"HyperText Transfer Protocol 2\",\"HyperText Transfer Protocol 2\",\"HyperText Transfer Protocol 2\",\"HyperText Transfer Protocol 2\",]`\n\nAfter this change, we generate the following JSON (shortened for clarity):\n\n```json\n\"http2\": [\n         \"HyperText Transfer Protocol 2\",\n          {\n            \"http2.stream\": {\n              \"http2.length\": \"43\",\n...\n              \"image-gif.end\": \"\"\n            }\n          },\n          {\n            \"http2.stream\": {\n              \"http2.length\": \"250\",\n              \"http2.type\": \"1\",\n              \"http2.flags\": \"0x04\",\n...\n                  \"http2.header.unescaped\": \"gzip\",\n                  \"http2.header.repr\": \"Indexed Header Field\",\n                  \"http2.header.index\": \"70\"\n                }\n              ]\n            }\n          },\n          \"HyperText Transfer Protocol 2\"\n        ]\n```",
  "state": "merged",
  "created_at": "2021-05-02T09:46:06.958Z",
